# Apache's default mod_mime Content-Type for .js/.css has no charset
# parameter, unlike PHP-served .html (which correctly sends charset=UTF-8).
# Without this, some browsers/proxies can misinterpret this theme's UTF-8
# source (e.g. German umlauts in src/i18n/de.js) as a different encoding.
AddCharset UTF-8 .js .css
